<urn:atm:triage:finding/QA-BB-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "QA-BB-001" ;
  triage:title "BB6-028's log_failure() outcome= fix has no regression-test coverage in storage_and_nudge_router.rs" ;
  triage:description "rust-qa-agent, BB-GATE-RERUN-1789285688 (phase-ending gate re-run, PR #1477, report 2026-09-13T10:40:00Z), fenix-verified at integrate/phase-bb @ 4cb8be1ce. BB6-028's fix added outcome = \"failed\" to prompt_handoff_record.rs's log_failure() tracing::error! call (confirmed present at line 88), but the Rust test harness that asserts this log call's fields (PromptHandoffErrorFields/PromptHandoffErrorEvent in crates/atm-http-runtime/src/storage_and_nudge_router.rs:1183-1224, and assert_prompt_handoff_error() :2138-2150) does not capture or assert an outcome field at all -- independently confirmed by direct read: the struct's 8 captured fields (subsystem/action/reason/message_id/kind/trigger/error_code/error) omit outcome. Same class of gap as the already-fixed BB6-029 (doc/smoke test with zero regression protection): the code fix is correct, but nothing in the automated Rust suite would catch a regression if outcome were dropped again." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-bb" ;
  triage:triageMode "phase_end" ;
  triage:category "testing" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:source "rust-qa-agent, verified by quality-mgr, BB-GATE-RERUN-1789285688 phase-ending gate re-run" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/storage_and_nudge_router.rs:1183-1224 (PromptHandoffErrorFields/PromptHandoffErrorEvent), ~2138-2151 (assert_prompt_handoff_error)" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-13T08:23:12Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "Lead ruling (2026-09-13, team-lead): important, not a reopening of the closed BB6-028 (the code fix itself remains correct and verified) -- a new, narrower regression-coverage gap in the same fix. Filed as its own record so the two stay individually accountable, same pattern used for BB6-028 vs BB6-026. CLOSED (2026-09-13T08:47:00Z): quality-mgr BB-GATE2-QA1-1789288411 (PR #1485, report 01M2CZ2MNJ14WHNB6FW75G1CS4) confirms fixed at fix/bb-gate2-findings @ 39850f06c -- outcome field + assertion added, 71/71 storage_and_nudge_router tests pass; quality-mgr personally ran a live mutation experiment removing the outcome field and confirmed all 5 assertion sites fail as expected, then reverted cleanly, proving the guard is genuine not vacuous." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BB6 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-13T08:23:12Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/QA-BB-001/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/QA-BB-001/2> ;
  triage:hasResolution <urn:atm:triage:resolution/QA-BB-001/1> ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-13T08:47:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

